        <title type="html"><![CDATA[MIDI APIs now use `NotAllowedError` instead of `InvalidAccessError`]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42334</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42334"/>
        <updated>2025-12-10T09:00:45.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29357907?u=5b1be4accbf0796916d326a344e5c36655396dde&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">Quoted from <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3712387494" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/WebAudio/web-midi-api/issues/278" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/WebAudio/web-midi-api/pull/278/hovercard" href="https://github.com/WebAudio/web-midi-api/pull/278">WebAudio/web-midi-api#278</a> PR description:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">According to <a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#invalidaccesserror" rel="nofollow">Web IDL spec on <code class="notranslate">InvalidAccessError</code></a>:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Deprecated. Use <a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#exceptiondef-typeerror" rel="nofollow">TypeError</a> for invalid arguments, "<a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#notsupportederror" rel="nofollow">NotSupportedError</a>" <a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-DOMException" rel="nofollow">DOMException</a> for unsupported operations, and "<a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#notallowederror" rel="nofollow">NotAllowedError</a>" <a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-DOMException" rel="nofollow">DOMException</a> for denied requests instead.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Previously, while trying to open <code class="notranslate">MIDIPort</code>, <code class="notranslate">"InvalidAccessError" DOMException</code> was thrown when...</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">the device is unavailable (e.g., is already in use by another process and cannot be opened, or is disconnected)</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">In this case, I believe <code class="notranslate">NotAllowedError</code> fits well, according to its <a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#notallowederror" rel="nofollow">Web IDL spec  description</a>:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">The request is not allowed by the user agent or the platform in the current context, possibly because the user denied permission.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Security and permissions reasons are only a subset of the appropriate causes, according to this definition. An attempt to <code class="notranslate">open</code> the port can fail. Somebody's exclusive lock on the port, or the port being disconnected, <ins>is</ins> the <ins>current context</ins> driving the platform's decision not to allow the operation.</p>
<p dir="auto">And in the context of forbidden <code class="notranslate">.send</code> calls:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">If data is a <a href="https://webaudio.github.io/web-midi-api/#dfn-system-exclusive" rel="nofollow">System Exclusive</a> message, and the <a href="https://webaudio.github.io/web-midi-api/#dom-midiaccess" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">MIDIAccess</code></a> did not enable <a href="https://webaudio.github.io/web-midi-api/#dfn-system-exclusive" rel="nofollow">System Exclusive</a> access, throw an <code class="notranslate">InvalidAccessError</code> exception.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto"><code class="notranslate">NotAllowedError</code> fits even better, because it fits an explicitly defined subset of permission errors.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto">The change in spec: <a class="commit-link" data-hovercard-type="commit" data-hovercard-url="https://github.com/WebAudio/web-midi-api/commit/3795f22/hovercard" href="https://github.com/WebAudio/web-midi-api/commit/3795f22">WebAudio/web-midi-api@<tt>3795f22</tt></a></p>
<p dir="auto">This PR should not be confused with <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3628538760" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41956" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/41956/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41956">#41956</a>, which talks about <code class="notranslate">SecurityError</code>s instead</p>]]></content>
